@end menu

@node Contributing
@section How To Contribute To This Manual

The Texinfo chapters live under @file{info/}; the current project overview and
installation summary live in @file{Readme.org} and @file{etc/install.org}.
Submit changes through the Emacsvox repository at
@url{https://github.com/bartbunting/emacsvox}.  Read @file{AGENTS.md} before
building or testing: Emacsvox requires Emacs 31 or newer and repository-local
@file{local.mk} selects the compiler used by supported targets.

Do not hand-edit generated references.  @file{info/docs.texi} and
@file{info/keys.texi} come from the source documentation generator;
@file{etc/aural-presentation-reference.org} comes from
@file{utils/emacsvox-aural-audit.el}.

@node Authoring Guidelines
@section Authoring Guidelines

Keep current operating instructions separate from historical accounts.  State
which back end or platform a procedure applies to, avoid duplicating detailed
protocol contracts across repositories, and link to the owning document.
Run @command{make docs-generate} after editing Texinfo, then run
@command{make docs-check}.  Commit the regenerated @file{emacsvox.info} files
with their source changes.

@subsection Publishing The Browser Manual

Texinfo on @code{master} is the canonical manual source.  GitHub Pages serves
the generated static files committed on the separate @code{gh-pages} branch;
never edit those HTML files as source.  Publishing is deliberately explicit:

@enumerate
@item
Finish the manual change, run the generation and validation targets above,
and commit the complete source-side change on @code{master}.

@item
Check out that exact commit in a clean source worktree.  Build its local,
ignored byte-code with the Emacs selected by @file{local.mk} or an
@code{EMACS=} override.  Use a separate sibling worktree checked out on
@code{gh-pages} as the publication directory.

@item
From the clean source worktree, run:

@example
make docs-publish-pages DOCS_PUBLISH_DIR=/path/to/emacsvox-pages
@end example

The target validates the manual, replaces only its managed HTML files, writes
@file{.nojekyll}, and records the source commit, Emacs version, and Texinfo
version in @file{emacsvox-source.txt}.  It refuses an uncommitted source tree.

@item
Inspect the @code{gh-pages} worktree, including the provenance file and the
main browser entry points.  Commit the generated site with the source commit
in the commit message, then push @code{master} and @code{gh-pages}.  The GitHub
Pages source setting must name the root of @code{gh-pages}.
@end enumerate

No documentation target creates a commit or pushes a branch.  This keeps the
published bytes reviewable and makes publication a distinct maintainer action.

